{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question","id":413424,"title":"Hatewheel has a Lunar question!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-20T17:17:01-08:00","id":413424,"title":"Hatewheel has a Lunar question!","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hatewheel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a query for anybody who feels like participating.<br /> <br /> List if you can, every problem you can think of with a shapeshifting power that allows a Lunar to change their features, but only their human features. With this power, the Lunar may change their entire appearance, even their gender, but they may not change themselves to impersonate another character. Describe all the problems with this. I'll be back in a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Link to RPG.net post: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?749241-Lunar-Exalted-What-Are-They-to-You&amp;p=18759676#post18759676\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...6#post18759676</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:25:48-08:00","id":413453,"title":"","content":"&quot;Problems&quot;, hmm. Problems.<br /> <br /> Presumably, this Charm cannot change the Lunar's Tell (or the pattern of their Tattoos, which will be assumed as included in &quot;the Tell&quot; for the rest of this post). So long as the Lunar's Tell remains unchanged, anyone who knows the Tell can recognize the Lunar regardless of any number of permanent changes to her true human shape. Though continuously changing her true human face can make it harder for someone to attach a specific identity and history of association with the Lunar, if they failed to notice the Tell in previous encounters or fail to see it in later ones.<br /> <br /> Essentially, this Charm is just a really good disguise Charm -- like Solar Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise, only without the mote-commitment or any need for make-up or props.<br /> <br /> A clever Lunar can, of course, assume an appearance plausibly close to that of someone another character has heard of but has never personally met. For example, a Dynastic mortal comes to Nexus looking to make a deal with a slave-owner known to have dark skin, red-hair and a thick Nexus accent. The Lunar can become a dark-skinned, red-headed man and speak with a thick Nexus accent, and even though the slave-owners associates would be able to spot the fake instantly, the Dynastic costumer can be fooled into thinking the Lunar is the man he's looking for.<br /> <br /> Especially if the Lunar uses social influence Charms to affect how others see her (the Lunar).<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing any &quot;problems&quot;. Rather, I do hope we see a return of Shaping the Ideal Form!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:30:52-08:00","id":413456,"title":"","content":"The only problem I can see is that it would mean that the Lunar would still have to Hunt, kill, eat a human or fuck them if they have that charm in order to perfectly imitate their shape, and that's only a problem with certain character types and a mitigatable one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:42:23-08:00","id":413483,"title":"","content":"Oh, I forgot something obvious!<br /> <br /> Shaping the Ideal Form doesn't prevent the Lunar from layering a MUNDANE disguise over their altered appearance, and the mundane disguise rules probably allow for the possibility of looking exactly like a specific person. It's legendarily difficult, but theoretically possible in some limited cases.<br /> <br /> With Shaping the Ideal Form UNlimiting the cases where mundane make-up could approximate a specific person's exact appearance, a Lunar with a sufficient Larceny rating and make-up kit wouldn't need to take Heart's Blood in order to look enough like someone to fool even their friends... under casual, distant scrutiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:44:26-08:00","id":413484,"title":"","content":"Sounds useful enough. I mean I assume the lack of being able to look exactly like a specific person just means I can't decide to look like someone I can think of and not some weird cosmic lock out that prevents me from a certain appearance because somewhere there is a person who looks like that. (I would so punch my ST if they pulled that.) It sounds kind of like the shadow disguise charm infernals had in second aside from clothing not being thrown into the shift. If you can't control your voice I would assume you'd be stuck with your impersonations whereas being able to alter that as well would negate that issue. I'm not seeing much of an issue with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:52:12-08:00","id":413487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question#post413424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Link to RPG.net post: <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?749241-Lunar-Exalted-What-Are-They-to-You&amp;p=18759676#post18759676\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?...6#post18759676</a></div> </div> </div> </div>All of my issues are language-based. What constitutes a human feature, given that most animals share body parts? Can you shape into a human with major birth defects? Wyld taint? Animal or supernatural heritage? What if your character has those to begin with? Also, gender isn't a physical quality: that would be sex. And the distinction about not being able to impersonate other people makes absolutely no sense from a fluff perspective and is obviously trying to neuter this power's utility in a really meta-gamey way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When Heaven forbids Exigents, only forbidden gods will have Exigents. <b>The Hanged Man wrote:</b> Space. Pfft, whatever. I can kick Space's ass with a starting Dynast.","edited":{"userid":716,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","user":"Capybara!","date":". 02-20-2015, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","name":"Capybara!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:52:45-08:00","id":413488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413484#post413484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume the lack of being able to look exactly like a specific person just means I can't decide to look like someone I can think of and not some weird cosmic lock out that prevents me from a certain appearance because somewhere there is a person who looks like that. (I would so punch my ST if they pulled that.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the problem currently being discussed over at RPG.net, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:59:59-08:00","id":413509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Capybara!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413487#post413487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the distinction about not being able to impersonate other people makes absolutely no sense from a fluff perspective and is obviously trying to neuter this power's stealth utility in a really meta-gamey way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the notion is that if you want to look exactly like a certain person, you should figure out a way to take their Heart's Blood - whether or not they survive that experience being up to you and the vagaries of your plot.<br /> <br /> This power seems a lot like Changing Plumage Mastery. As in, very useful when you arrive in a new place to blend in and not look like an outsider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:01:32-08:00","id":413512,"title":"","content":"I don't have an easy answer myself.<br /> <br /> As he points out, that kind of arbitrary identity-lock makes sense for a Second Edition Ebon Dragon Charm, which alters reality according to a concept rather than operating purely through physical transformation.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, what stops a Solar using Second Edition Flawless Impenetrable Disguise from mimicking the appearance of a specific other person? The Solar isn't working on reality-altering conceptual levels, but is using physical make-up and props and reality-bending skill. If the Solar can look like someone else, she can look like ANYONE in particular. (At least, within the limited range of changes that Charm allows. It can only alter her apparent age, size and build so far, and not actually change her gender at all.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, I think I do have an easy answer!<br /> <br /> Okay, assuming you will NOT impose a magical limitation of &quot;Shaping the Ideal From cannot mimic someone else's exact appearance&quot;, then I would allow a Lunar to use it to appear like someone even without their Heart's Blood, but the Lunar's Tell is REALLY OBVIOUS. That way the Lunar can appear exactly like someone, but in a way that the disguise is still very imperfect, and in a way that encourages the Lunar to take Heart's Blood for a properly flawless disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:03:20-08:00","id":413514,"title":"","content":"@Zelbinnean<br /> <br /> Sure, I could see that as necessary for a perfect imitation, but what about a good disguise? What if my Lunar took dots in Larceny? Why if my Lunar didn't take dots in Larceny, but still wants to walk around looking like that sweet girl from the tea house?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When Heaven forbids Exigents, only forbidden gods will have Exigents. <b>The Hanged Man wrote:</b> Space. Pfft, whatever. I can kick Space's ass with a starting Dynast.","edited":{"userid":716,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","user":"Capybara!","date":". 02-20-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","name":"Capybara!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:04:28-08:00","id":413515,"title":"","content":"This is what I suggested the Changing Moons anima power should be in another thread, though I also added clause that this shape-shifting cannot be combined with hearts blood shape-shifting charms.<br /> <br /> The one problem that immediately comes to mind is how do you balance the sheer utility of being able to take on any face you like. The way the charm is worded above I would say not being able to take known faces is a key balance, yes you can make yourself look like a typical merchant or sea captain, but you cant benefit from taking the shape of a particular person and using all the associations people make when seeing that person. You are generic sea captain #3 not Cinder Beard the Merciless Scourge of the Inner Sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:05:20-08:00","id":413516,"title":"","content":"You could just make yourself look almost exactly like someone except that you have a spot. That's the problem I had with the Ebon Dragon charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:08:09-08:00","id":413519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>turkeygiant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413515#post413515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one problem that immediately comes to mind is how do you balance the sheer utility of being able to take on any face you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars get to do that, no problem (through impersonation/Larceny).<br /> <br /> Buuuuut they're also Solars, of course.<br /> <br /> It does make sense that Lunars would have to approach this differently. I'm not sold on a super-visible Tell - that would basically negate the benefit.<br /> <br /> And Wiz is also right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Capybara!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413514#post413514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I could see that as necessary for a perfect imitation, but what about a good disguise? What if my Lunar took dots in Larceny? Why if my Lunar didn't take dots in Larceny, but still wants to walk around looking like that sweet girl from the tea house?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those all sound like great reasons to finagle some Heart's Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:08:40-08:00","id":413521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413516#post413516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just make yourself look almost exactly like someone except that you have a spot. That's the problem I had with the Ebon Dragon charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a DM though I would swat the player trying to do that as it is obviously not in the spirit of the charms limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:09:22-08:00","id":413524,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the rule is not reasonable and falls apart under small scrutiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When Heaven forbids Exigents, only forbidden gods will have Exigents. <b>The Hanged Man wrote:</b> Space. Pfft, whatever. I can kick Space's ass with a starting Dynast.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/716-capybara","name":"Capybara!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:30:46-08:00","id":413558,"title":"","content":"There's also a problem with &quot;human features&quot; mentioned already. Beastmen are considered to be human - so are wyld mutants, Do human variants (like Djala or air people) qualify as well? If not, why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T18:46:15-08:00","id":413582,"title":"","content":"The &quot;No mimicing actual persons&quot;-thing is familiar to... well, most D&amp;D players who care for shapechangers and illusionists. Those abilities usually call out if you can transform into &quot;a human, but no individuals&quot; in general, or &quot;a specific human individual decided by you&quot; - the only ability that actually does the later is the Doppelganger's shape change, as far as I remember.<br /> <br /> Buuut, that's technically irrelevant. Back to Exalted.<br /> It helps if you rationalise it as &quot;The charm is not precise enough to mimic other people&quot;. As in, sure, you can disguise yourself as someone else, but then it's just &quot;magical disguise (that happens to resemble someone)&quot;, not &quot;perfectly copying the form&quot;. How good the likeness is depends on how good your largency + whatever (manipulation?) roll is, and anyone with enough perception + awareness can spot the differences - those familiar with the person even get bonuses on this.<br /> <br /> (For that matter, <sub>that's how I run these kind of restrictions in D&amp;D</sub>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 02-20-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T20:46:02-08:00","id":413653,"title":"","content":"I like the general idea of 'you can try to mimic someone else without their hearts blood but you have to make a disguise role to see how convincing your attempt to mimic them was'.<br /> <br /> Like, for example, that time in Fullmetal Alchemist when the shape shifting Envy got called out as a fake because they forgot a detail ( a mole on the cheek) and the person they were trying to trick was observant enough to notice the flaw. Shape shifting doesn't help if you screw up on what the details of the person you are turning into actually are.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, another example of that kind of thing was in the early part of the Naruto series. Someone was trying to mimic a character using the transformation jutsu but they messed up on the details (left out a recent wound and wearing their weapons pouch on the wrong side) and got caught.<br /> <br /> Edit Edit: And, of course, it would be nearly impossible to actually mimic someone you never met because you either have no idea what they look like or only have second hand information from other people that may or may not be accurate. At that point getting it right would be more a matter of sheer dumb luck then actual skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 02-20-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T21:10:31-08:00","id":413687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413509#post413509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the notion is that if you want to look exactly like a certain person, you should figure out a way to take their Heart's Blood - whether or not they survive that experience being up to you and the vagaries of your plot.<br /> <br /> This power seems a lot like Changing Plumage Mastery. As in, very useful when you arrive in a new place to blend in and not look like an outsider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, somewhat, though <b>Changing Plumage Mastery</b> only allows you to cosmetically alter <i>learned shapes </i>to a limited degree.<br /> <br /> It's more like <b>Perfection of the Mockingbird</b>, in that you alter your <i>true shape</i>, with no need to canablise anyone just to be able to look <i>inconspicuous</i>. (Although <i>that</i> requires you to supplement a disguise action.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T21:46:09-08:00","id":413728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413687#post413687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, somewhat, though <b>Changing Plumage Mastery</b> only allows you to cosmetically alter <i>learned shapes </i>to a limited degree.<br /> <br /> It's more like <b>Perfection of the Mockingbird</b>, in that you alter your <i>true shape</i>, with no need to canablise anyone just to be able to look <i>inconspicuous</i>. (Although <i>that</i> requires you to supplement a disguise action.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. I was going to say, between that Knack and Charm, Lunars could already do this in 2nd edition. So I don't see why they shouldn't be able to do this in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T22:18:07-08:00","id":413804,"title":"","content":"I think most of the benefits of using this charm for disguises is in ignoring penalties. If my fair skinned, fair haired, Lunar lady wants to impersonate a specific swarthy, dark haired sailor guy who's twice her size, she's gonna have hella penalties on that disguise roll. Size, gender, complexion, to name a few.<br /> <br /> this charm lets her ignore those penalties by actually becoming a swarthy sailor guy who's twice her size. Then her disguise roll covers the last few details to get the specific person she's going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Life before Death, Strength before Weakness, Journey before Destination.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">&quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves&quot;</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4172-marros56","name":"Marros56","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4172_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T22:19:36-08:00","id":413805,"title":"","content":"1. Fluff-wise, there's no reason the ability to change your own shape to your specifications shouldn't let you copy someone. The idea that a Lunar who just wants an attractive form to wear for a nice night out can sit in front of a mirror and be all, &quot;Let's see, I'm gonna give myself gorgeous long red hair, and a stern face, and piercing green eyes, and a nice figure with a bit of muscle, and some awesome breasts, and to top it all off I want a smooth and regal bearing&quot; can do what she wants, but she can't sit in front of a mirror with a portrait and use the same power to disguise herself as the Scarlet Empress is bullshit. It's imposing a metagame rule for balance in such a way that it keeps things from making sense.<br /> <br /> 2. Mechanics-wise, it eliminates 9 out of 10 reasons you hunt a human with the Sacred Hunt. Most times you don't need to disguise yourself as a specific person, just as &quot;someone fitted to be where I am now.&quot; Most of the time you don't need to be the Scarlet Empress, you just need to be Imperial Mint Clerk #3. If you can be Imperial Mint Clerk #3 without having to hunt anyone, then you'll rarely ever have to hunt anyone, especially since the hunt is work. It incentivizes players to go with generic disguises rather than hunting someone and then impersonating them which is just narratively much cooler.<br /> <br /> 3. If you're looking for a way to fit into diverse cultures or not stick out like a sore thumb that doesn't also give a free perfect disguise superpower, look to the Lunar charms for being accepted as normal by social groups, not to the Lunar shapeshifting powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T22:26:55-08:00","id":413812,"title":"","content":"So basically you're suggesting giving Lunars the same human disguise/appearance customization potential that Alchemicals already have with Husk-Sculpting Apparatus?<br /> <br /> I'm with Sunder, I see nothing wrong with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T23:10:53-08:00","id":413842,"title":"","content":"Will the sex change be purely cosmetic?<br /> <br /> Will my fake penis be able to become erect, will it be able to ejaculate, and will the ejaculated fluids be functional sperm capable of siring children?<br /> <br /> Will I get ovaries when turning into a woman? What happens if I use it while pregnant? <br /> <br /> None of these questions are jokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T01:26:33-08:00","id":413910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413842#post413842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the sex change be purely cosmetic?<br /> <br /> Will my fake penis be able to become erect, will it be able to ejaculate, and will the ejaculated fluids be functional sperm capable of siring children?<br /> <br /> Will I get ovaries when turning into a woman? What happens if I use it while pregnant?<br /> <br /> None of these questions are jokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a Knack in 2E called Twin-Faced Hero that allowed a Lunar to change their true form's sex completely, not just to the opposite of their birth, but even to neuter. The changed form is fully functional in all respects, and errata stated that a Lunar would remain in child-bearing form until the baby is born.<br /> <br /> As to how this would relate to the proposed ability, I would guess the charm would either dovetail off of this Knack, or the Knack would be a requirement for changing one's sex with the new ability. Or, it could replace Twin-Faced Hero completely as the superior option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T01:30:36-08:00","id":413914,"title":"","content":"The disguise roll for specific people sounds like a good way to do it. Possibly it should just let you do the disguise roll at the speed of the charm (whatever that is) and without requiring props, but other than that be no better than anyone else trying to disguise themselves.<br /> <br /> Certainly, in my experience, saying &quot;you can't look like specific people&quot; with no details doesn't work well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T01:45:09-08:00","id":413916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413842#post413842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the sex change be purely cosmetic?<br /> <br /> Will my fake penis be able to become erect, will it be able to ejaculate, and will the ejaculated fluids be functional sperm capable of siring children?<br /> <br /> Will I get ovaries when turning into a woman? What happens if I use it while pregnant?<br /> <br /> None of these questions are jokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, they're good question actually. The <b>Twin Faced Hero</b> knack currently allows a Lunar to <i>fully-functionally </i>change any form to any sex (or none*). So how is this proposed charm meant to interact with that? Will it:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Require <b>Twin Faced Hero</b> as a prerequisite,</li> <li>Be a purely cosmetic sex change unless you also use <b>Twin Faced Hero</b>, or</li> <li>Simply replace <b>Twin Faced Hero</b> in the new edition, having subsumed its functionality.</li> </ol><span style=\"font-size:9px\">(* neuter functionality includes near perfect birth control -- hey, it's Creation, where even neuters and males can get pregnant. )<br /> <br /> ---</span><br /> <br /> PS: Being pregnant doesn't stop a Lunar from shape shifting, and it seems shape shifting doesn't stop a Lunar from being pregnant. ( Doing so <i>may</i> have side effects on the child though. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T06:18:36-08:00","id":413998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413842#post413842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the sex change be purely cosmetic?<br /> <br /> Will my fake penis be able to become erect, will it be able to ejaculate, and will the ejaculated fluids be functional sperm capable of siring children?<br /> <br /> Will I get ovaries when turning into a woman? What happens if I use it while pregnant? <br /> <br /> None of these questions are jokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think changing sex should be merely cosmetic (but convincing - a Lunar whose original human form has breasts and a vagina can turn them into a flat chest and a functional penis and testicles, but when they ejaculate they're sterile).<br /> <br /> Giving your false-form virility would require stronger magic or taking Heart's Blood and truly shape shifting rather than just donning a very convincing magic disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T07:34:14-08:00","id":414027,"title":"","content":"I don't visit RPGNET but as others mention:<br /> <br /> <b>Turning into Beastmen?</b> I can hass mutations for bonuses (or is it like Mystique copying Wolverine's claws - just flesh)?<br /> <br /> <b>Turning into God-Blooded? Terrestrial?</b> I can emulate signs of magical breeding, yes? Leaves in my hair? Can I breath smoke? What if I eat the heartsblood of a firebeetle or something, can I then breath smoke?<br /> <br /> Does it have to be an existing example -- could I become a<b> blue or purple</b> human?<br /> <br /> <b>Tattoos? </b>Demon-Blooded can take a mutation - a tattoo/sigil/birthmark - that lets other Demons know that the Demon-Blooded is claimed by someone (and to carelessly harass them would incur their wrath). Can a Lunar copy this birthmark or tattoo? On the same tangent, if I'm trying to blend into a society with extensive tattoos, how far can I go? In a Nordic tribe, would I have my own woads with plant motifs? Great. What about if the tattoos are <b>specific</b>?<br /> Forgive the example, but if a Lunar was sneaking into a Holocaust camp, could such a tattoo create numbers on their forearm (no need to copy anyone specific)? Or would it be a gibberish collection of letters and symbols that any guard would detect as fake? Likewise, in Creation, if I'm trying to masquerade as a slave, could I mimic a brand without actually being branded?<br /> <br /> *<br /> What about using this power to <b>copy myself</b>?<br /> <br /> What if I wanted to take my current form --- and make it look &quot;divine&quot;, so I could walk around like a god-blood (leave hair, bark skin, etc) --- and then pretend my non-elemental form was an illusion I use to not scare mortals?<br /> <br /> What if I wanted to take my current form &quot;as is&quot; --- so if (whatever deception detecting magics) broken, I revert to my &quot;true form&quot; (warform, animal, whatever) and people think my True Human form was merely an illusion?<br /> <br /> <b>What about injuries?</b><br /> <br /> What if I want to take a form (myself or other)..... <b>missing an arm, an eye, a leg? </b>How far can I emulate a cripple? Scars? Injuries? Will the local townsfolk slash their children's faces with knives because they think it'd discourage me from taking their souls (or more practically, because I can't mimic the scars and so would be easier to detect)?<br /> <br /> And<b> if I can emulate injuries - to what extent?</b> Can I &quot;bleed&quot; from an amputated arm (that I've absorbed into my torso)? Can I shapeshift scars on my stomach? If scars, then what about deeper wounds? If wounds, can I make them bleed? If bleeding, can it reach the bone?<b> Can I feign death?</b> Can I shift my organs around, within a sealed layer of flesh --- but on the outside, appear to have deep wounds that go through me? Ghost-Blooded? Nephwrack? Decay? How far can I emulate my own death?<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> <b>How about accents? Voices.</b> Our biology/physical affects our voices <i>just as much</i> as our culture/language. It's fair game to sound more masculine and feminine because of testosterone and such, yes? And if so, to what degree can we change our voices to sound different? Can we modify our voices to help us sound more like a native user ---- if I visit Chiaroscuro for the first time, and I'm from the far North, can I switch my voice around a little to help with pronunciation of strange letters or sounds?<br /> <br /> *<br /> <br /> <b>No mechanical benefits, I imagine? </b>So it's impossible to use this to gain the <b>Small or Large</b> mutations --- Lunars adults can't become children nor giants; Lunar children can't become adults, right?<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance </b>has always been the big one. It's a problematic stat. Are we saying an <b>Appearance 1</b> Lunar can shapeshift.... but everytime they do, they fuck it up and look hideous? Likewise, an <b>Appearance 5</b> Lunar cannot drop their <b>Appearance to 0</b> in order to terrify people or emulate an Abyssal?<br /> <b>What if</b> someone is &quot;only attracted to far-Western people&quot; -- and your Appearance 5 Western Lunar shifts to look like a far-Eastern person -- are we still required to be attracted to their Appearance 5? Likewise with North and South. <b>What does Appearance (in general) and especially to Lunars (given that they can hold the &quot;stat value&quot; while radically changing their looks).</b> If Desus could be disinterested in Lillith turning into masculine forms......how do other people, in social combat with a Lunar, say &quot;sorry, I know you purchased a high stat score, but I'm going to ignore that since I dislike what you are&quot;? With Lunar Shapeshifting, how can others react? What if my character thinks your &quot;Lunar from Harborhead&quot; <i>is fantastic</i> (so ok, penalties to socials for me) -- but then you shapeshift to look like someone from Whitewall and the pulse goes limp (you might as well have a penis). What if a Dynast finds your &quot;Lunar Patrician&quot; to be an <i>ideal</i> mate (and ok, they get suckered along) but then the Lunar shifts into a barbarian savage --- how do handle this fuzzy area where &quot;the Lunar has the<b> same stats</b> - but because they can shift, people will <b>react radically different</b>&quot;&quot;?<br /> <br /> etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","user":"SachKreiosLucy4","date":". 02-21-2015, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T11:43:49-08:00","id":414230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Appearance </b>has always been the big one. It's a problematic stat. Are we saying an <b>Appearance 1</b> Lunar can shapeshift.... but everytime they do, they fuck it up and look hideous? Likewise, an <b>Appearance 5</b> Lunar cannot drop their <b>Appearance to 0</b> in order to terrify people or emulate an Abyssal?<br /> <b>What if</b> someone is &quot;only attracted to far-Western people&quot; -- and your Appearance 5 Western Lunar shifts to look like a far-Eastern person -- are we still required to be attracted to their Appearance 5? Likewise with North and South. <b>What does Appearance (in general) and especially to Lunars (given that they can hold the &quot;stat value&quot; while radically changing their looks).</b> If Desus could be disinterested in Lillith turning into masculine forms......how do other people, in social combat with a Lunar, say &quot;sorry, I know you purchased a high stat score, but I'm going to ignore that since I dislike what you are&quot;? With Lunar Shapeshifting, how can others react? What if my character thinks your &quot;Lunar from Harborhead&quot; <i>is fantastic</i> (so ok, penalties to socials for me) -- but then you shapeshift to look like someone from Whitewall and the pulse goes limp (you might as well have a penis). What if a Dynast finds your &quot;Lunar Patrician&quot; to be an <i>ideal</i> mate (and ok, they get suckered along) but then the Lunar shifts into a barbarian savage --- how do handle this fuzzy area where &quot;the Lunar has the<b> same stats</b> - but because they can shift, people will <b>react radically different</b>&quot;&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Those are all &quot;problems&quot; with the Appearance attribute itself, if you choose to deal with them. Not problems with a minor shapeshifting disguise charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T11:49:30-08:00","id":414232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=414230#post414230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are all &quot;problems&quot; with the Appearance attribute itself, if you choose to deal with them. Not problems with a minor shapeshifting disguise charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed - hence why I prefaced it with &quot;Appearance is the big one&quot;.<br /> <br /> I feel it's worth bring up because Lunars are the ones who can &quot;flip the switch&quot; the most, <i>and repeatedly</i>, with this charm. That's all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4946-sachkreioslucy4","name":"SachKreiosLucy4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T12:26:44-08:00","id":414262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>No mechanical benefits, I imagine? </b>So it's impossible to use this to gain the <b>Small or Large</b> mutations --- Lunars adults can't become children nor giants; Lunar children can't become adults, right? </div> </div> </div>I don't see why a lunar shapeshifter who can turn into a mouse or a yeddim can't turn into a child or a giant, but then again you needed to buy knacks to do those things in 2E so maybe 3E will likewise also make it something you have to buy with XP to be able to do? In which case a lunar without those charms wouldn't be able to turn into a child or a giant but a lunar who had them would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T12:42:11-08:00","id":414309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SachKreiosLucy4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=414232#post414232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed - hence why I prefaced it with &quot;Appearance is the big one&quot;.<br /> <br /> I feel it's worth bring up because Lunars are the ones who can &quot;flip the switch&quot; the most, <i>and repeatedly</i>, with this charm. That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's also worth noting that any shapeshifting-disguise Charm might be Appearance-based.<br /> <br /> Unless it's a got a minimum Attribute requirement of 1, the Lunar is going to have some Appearance dots to use, which she may hide or reveal as she pleases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T13:55:07-08:00","id":414413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=414309#post414309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's also worth noting that any shapeshifting-disguise Charm might be Appearance-based.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, that feels much more Manipulation or Wits than Appearance to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T14:36:50-08:00","id":414448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=414413#post414413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, that feels much more Manipulation or Wits than Appearance to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not Manipulation.<br /> <br /> The Lunar isn't lying if this really is their new, true appearance. For them, changing gender or skin color would be like trying out a new hairstyle.<br /> <br /> Now hiding their Tell -- THAT would lying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T14:46:31-08:00","id":414455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413805#post413805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Mechanics-wise, it eliminates 9 out of 10 reasons you hunt a human with the Sacred Hunt. Most times you don't need to disguise yourself as a specific person, just as &quot;someone fitted to be where I am now.&quot; Most of the time you don't need to be the Scarlet Empress, you just need to be Imperial Mint Clerk #3. If you can be Imperial Mint Clerk #3 without having to hunt anyone, then you'll rarely ever have to hunt anyone, especially since the hunt is work. It incentivizes players to go with generic disguises rather than hunting someone and then impersonating them which is just narratively much cooler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, charm/knacks like this proposed power, the <i>current</i> Perfection of the Mockingbird, and sometimes the Changing Moon anima power do that.<br /> <br /> This is a <i>good</i> thing. Cannibal identity-theft is a narrative that should not be <i>trivialised</i> by requiring it just to give the Lunar quick disguises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 02-21-2015, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T14:51:32-08:00","id":414459,"title":"","content":"0. What is the purpose of this charm? Is it &quot;I want to look like not me&quot;, &quot;I want to look like I live in this area / like I am a foreigner&quot;, &quot;I want to be able to use shapeshifting to get part of the way to disguising myself as someone&quot;, &quot;I want to change my level of beauty&quot;, &quot;I want to look like a general type of person&quot;? Depending on your design goal, &quot;don't look like a specific person&quot; might or might not matter. Appearance might not matter, or it might be the only reason to use this charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. I want to mostly look like me, but different enough that people won't recognize me. Or close enough that I will look like a sibling, or a twin, or an older/younger version of myself. How do you mechanically handle &quot;I want to look this percentage like someone&quot;<br /> 2. As written, you should be able to impersonate someone's features, but it should take time and depend on your references. If you work from a photo of Hatewheel, it should be harder than if you follow Hatewheel around for a week and update your features as you watch him.<br /> 3. Is mass conserved? <br /> 4. Is there a difference between &quot;the way a person moves&quot; and &quot;physical features that influence movement&quot;? If I try to make myself as fat as Negazer, will I have trouble walking? Does this let me imitate a supermodel's strut? What about imitating the movement of King Edward (super-extreme scoliosis, it was basically physically impossible for him to stand up straight). Can I imitate the way a martial artist walks if I'm not a martial artist. If you can't imitate how someone moves, how does that affect disguise difficulty?<br /> 5. Is this a &quot;puff of smoke and you look different&quot;, or a &quot;push and pinch your face like molding clay&quot; transformation? The puff of smoke is probably easier to rein in since you can't go back and 'improve' your transformation.<br /> <br /> A roundabout way of &quot;no copying someone&quot; might be, say, you can use this to look like a generic person of country, or some region that has a single god. But then would all Lunars look the same if they shift into &quot;form of Great Forks&quot;?<br /> What if there is a specific, limited palette of changes (a la MMORPG character creation)? Say you can change hair length, hair color can ONLY be blonde, red, or brunette, skin can only be one of 4 skin tones?<br /> <br /> Actually, Luna has what 5 primary forms? Would limiting this charm to &quot;5 forms that are alternate yous&quot; work? Maybe also letting you remove one alternate you and replace it with another alternate you every so often? It gives a good reason for not imitating specific people, gives you enough forms that you can survive someone revealing secret identity #2 by switching to id #3, and a swap-out rule would let you move from far South to far North, and get rid of forms that would stick out like a sore thumb. I'm reminded of Moorcock's Eternal Champion. Also gives a reason for Appearance not changing.<br /> <br /> I would also want to know if this is meant to be a quick, temporary change (Sherlock in the 1st movie disguising as a beggar), longterm sleeper agent, or something in between (Mission Impossible disguise would last for a scene or two).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:03:10-08:00","id":414472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=414455#post414455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, charm/knacks like this proposed power, the <i>current</i> Perfection of the Mockingbird, and sometimes the Changing Moon anima power do that.<br /> <br /> This is a <i>good</i> thing. Cannibal identity-theft is a narrative that should not be <i>trivialised</i> by requiring it just to give the Lunar quick disguises.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all you need is a quick disguise then I would be very frustrated if effects like &quot;look like the person your target most expects/look like the person your target most wants to see/look like a generic blend of everyone around you to those not looking super close&quot; are deemed &quot;too illusion-y to be Properly Lunar.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T16:48:48-08:00","id":414611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413805#post413805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Fluff-wise, there's no reason the ability to change your own shape to your specifications shouldn't let you copy someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, and it has been already mentioned in this thread - the ability may not have the required precision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413805#post413805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that a Lunar who just wants an attractive form to wear for a nice night out can sit in front of a mirror and be all, &quot;Let's see, I'm gonna give myself gorgeous long red hair, and a stern face, and piercing green eyes, and a nice figure with a bit of muscle, and some awesome breasts, and to top it all off I want a smooth and regal bearing&quot; can do what she wants, but she can't sit in front of a mirror with a portrait and use the same power to disguise herself as the Scarlet Empress is bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? The fact that someone can paint a good portrait doesn't mean automatically, that they are able to make a perfect duplicate of Mona Lisa.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=413805#post413805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Mechanics-wise, it eliminates 9 out of 10 reasons you hunt a human with the Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Less than that, although i do agree that impersonation <i>is</i> an important reason why someone might want to look as a different human. In my experience, however, i found that a lot of people wanted human shapes just in order to have an ability to <b>not</b> be recognized. And in that case temporary shapes not tied to any specific person would do even better than Hunting someone at random. And that's even without going into moral considerations.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T22:11:34-08:00","id":414911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=414309#post414309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's also worth noting that any shapeshifting-disguise Charm might be Appearance-based.<br /> <br /> Unless it's a got a minimum Attribute requirement of 1, the Lunar is going to have some Appearance dots to use, which she may hide or reveal as she pleases.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=414413#post414413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, that feels much more Manipulation or Wits than Appearance to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=414448#post414448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely not Manipulation.<br /> <br /> The Lunar isn't lying if this really is their new, true appearance. For them, changing gender or skin color would be like trying out a new hairstyle.<br /> <br /> Now hiding their Tell -- THAT would lying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Charms for <i>Disguise</i> currently fall under Appearance, <i>Camouflage </i>under Wits, and <i>Impersonation</i> under Manipulation.<br /> <br /> So Appearance is the most likely candidate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T11:10:24-08:00","id":760087,"title":"","content":"Revisiting this question in light of the corebook's preliminary rules on The Tell.<br /> <br /> For the record, the rule is that the Lunar's Tell is plainly obvious in his human form, and only someone who has seen the Tell has the opportunity to spot the Tell in ANY other form, which requires being suspicious enough to make a &quot;Detect/Pierce Disguise&quot; action (page 224) with a dice roll of Perception + Awareness at a flat difficulty of 7.<br /> <br /> <br /> Using a Charm to copy someone (or some<i>thing</i>) else's appearance without Heart's Blood can be balanced by making the Lunar's Tell more obvious in that guise; anywhere from &quot;just as plainly obvious as in his human form&quot; to as something as simple as &quot;you still have to make the same check, but you don't need to have seen the Tell before&quot;, with various gradations in between.<br /> <br /> It's also balanced by the fact that the Lunar is only gaining the target's appearance, and none of their dice-pools or any of Charm-derived advantages that trigger off of Heart's Blood, such as potentially recalling memories, stealing magical attunements to distant manses, or assuming the thread of their Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T20:33:37-08:00","id":761180,"title":"","content":"I'd honestly have an easier time justifying &quot;you can alter your appearance, but cannot look identical to another specific person&quot; for Sidereals than for Lunars. If the Lunar can mold their flesh as they choose, why shouldn't they be able to mold it in those patterns? With a Sidereal you could better justify it with stuff like &quot;by adopting strands of unused possibilities in the Loom of Fate&quot; &quot;the character can not assume a possible appearance that Fate has assigned to a different person&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T20:46:50-08:00","id":761190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761180#post761180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd honestly have an easier time justifying &quot;you can alter your appearance, but cannot look identical to another specific person&quot; for Sidereals than for Lunars. If the Lunar can mold their flesh as they choose, why shouldn't they be able to mold it in those patterns? With a Sidereal you could better justify it with stuff like &quot;by adopting strands of unused possibilities in the Loom of Fate&quot; &quot;the character can not assume a possible appearance that Fate has assigned to a different person&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.<br /> <br /> What do you think about my idea above?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T20:50:35-08:00","id":761197,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't see why looking like a specific person is a problem. If a Solar, a DB, or even a Mortal, can use mundane disguises to look like a specific person, why can a Lunar not shapeshift to do so? It does not devalue Heart's Blood, because you have to roll Int + Larceny every time to get it right, just like a standard disguise, unless you actually have their heart's blood. The disguise aspect, to me, would be a secondary concern for the sheer coolness of being able to cosmetically sculpt your appearance at will.<br /> <br /> If that's still too edging on HB for some people, then go with Sunder's idea, and make the Tell stand out more when you're obviously not looking like yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T20:53:54-08:00","id":761199,"title":"","content":"my honest thinking is a fixed Changing Moon Anima Power resolves the need for a Charm to do the same thing, and while that may minorly disadvantage No Moons and Full Moons (though hopefully their own Anima powers would make up for it), the &quot;casual trickster&quot; allowance to bypass the Sacred Hunt to assume an illusory form, is much more solidly in the Changing Moon's thematic wheel house compared to theirs.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say your suggestion wouldn't be balanced, I just don't know how thematically necessary it would be before getting a better view of 3E Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T20:59:01-08:00","id":761204,"title":"","content":"I just want Lunars to have a version of Husk-Sculpting Mechanism from 2e Alchemicals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:14:49-08:00","id":761214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761199#post761199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my honest thinking is a fixed Changing Moon Anima Power resolves the need for a Charm to do the same thing, and while that may minorly disadvantage No Moons and Full Moons (though hopefully their own Anima powers would make up for it), the &quot;casual trickster&quot; allowance to bypass the Sacred Hunt to assume an illusory form, is much more solidly in the Changing Moon's thematic wheel house compared to theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas I think that &quot;disguise&quot; isn't any more inherently Changing Moon than the others, and would prefer Changing Moons to get something that enhances their ability to scare and/or seduce people. Or perhaps an effect to increase their Guile against scrutiny, possibly with an effect to help them overcome other people's Guile?<br /> <br /> You know what happened the last time the developers made the Changing Moons better shapeshifters than the other two Castes? Everyone playing First Edition was shoehorning Full Moon and No Moon character concepts into Changing Moons.<br /> <br /> Because people play Lunars to be shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761204#post761204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want Lunars to have a version of Husk-Sculpting Mechanism from 2e Alchemicals. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Back in my day, we called that Shaping the Ideal Form.<br /> <br /> First Edition Lunars could make their true forms look however they wanted, except for the Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-09-2015, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:17:29-08:00","id":761215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761214#post761214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas I think that &quot;disguise&quot; isn't any more inherently Changing Moon than the others, and would prefer Changing Moons to get something that enhances their ability to scare and/or seduce people.<br /> <br /> You know what happened the last time the developers made the Changing Moons better shapeshifters than the other two Castes? Everyone playing First Edition was shoehorning Full Moon and No Moon character concepts into Changing Moons.<br /> <br /> Because people play Lunars to be shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, agreed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761214#post761214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in my day, we called that Shaping the Ideal Form.<br /> <br /> First Edition Lunars could make their true forms look however they wanted, except for the Tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did that go away?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:24:47-08:00","id":761221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761215#post761215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did that go away?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it didn't entirely vanish.<br /> <br /> Part of it lived on in Twin-Faced Hero.<br /> <br /> ...Yeah, I have no idea why, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:47:37-08:00","id":761234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761221#post761221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it didn't entirely vanish.<br /> <br /> Part of it lived on in Twin-Faced Hero.<br /> <br /> ...Yeah, I have no idea why, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Plumage Mastery, actually, but it was weird for human shapes in that it could alter clothing but not a lot of other things that StIF could..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:55:01-08:00","id":761241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761234#post761234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing Plumage Mastery, actually, but it was weird for human shapes in that it could alter clothing but not a lot of other things that StIF could..</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right. I forgot that Changing Plummage was sort of Shaping the Ideal Form... for anything BUT your true form. I only remembered that it altered clothes, and maybe hair.<br /> <br /> Still, I remember being confused about why the two Charm/Knacks were separated, and the rest of StIF was left out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T00:23:18-08:00","id":761283,"title":"","content":"Yay, Lunars!<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's a bit silly to not be able to look like someone. Just make this a disguise-aiding charm as well.<br /> <br /> More serious concern with the language used though: gender is not sex. Please make sure to get those distinctions right.<br /> <br /> And (very) related to this Charm, as Lunars are obviously stll the primary &quot;genderbending&quot; splat (one of the reasons I love them), please acknowledge the existence of gender-dysphoria. Don't make a big deal out of it, just say that in reality it's really no fun to have a gender-identity which doesn't match your sex, but Lunars don't suffer from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T09:09:14-08:00","id":761540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761283#post761283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More serious concern with the language used though: gender is not sex. Please make sure to get those distinctions right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe when English provides a word for &quot;what genitalia you have&quot; which isn't the exact same word as &quot;intercourse&quot;, I'll start to use that word to label someone by their dangly bits instead of &quot;gender&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-09-2015, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T15:43:30-08:00","id":761773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761540#post761540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe when English provides a word for &quot;what genitalia you have&quot; which isn't the exact same word as &quot;intercourse&quot;, I'll start to use that word to label someone by their dangly bits instead of &quot;gender&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be like that. If context ever gets confused, you can add extra words on to denote whether or not it's intercourse or dangly bits (gametes and what produces them, really) themselves. That's why English has terms like &quot;sex(ual) position&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T16:19:24-08:00","id":761810,"title":"","content":"This may be kind of weird, but... based on limited play experience, I have a feeling that many (not all, not by a long shot, but a lot, maybe most) Lunars who take that knack wind up as gender-fluid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T02:03:41-08:00","id":762104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=761199#post761199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my honest thinking is a fixed Changing Moon Anima Power resolves the need for a Charm to do the same thing, and while that may minorly disadvantage No Moons and Full Moons (though hopefully their own Anima powers would make up for it), the &quot;casual trickster&quot; allowance to bypass the Sacred Hunt to assume an illusory form, is much more solidly in the Changing Moon's thematic wheel house compared to theirs.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say your suggestion wouldn't be balanced, I just don't know how thematically necessary it would be before getting a better view of 3E Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to check the backer pdf again, but I do know that in 2E all Solars had &quot;universal&quot; anima powers like lighting up the area or knowing the time. Perhaps a temporary illusion like this could be something similar for 3E Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T02:09:14-08:00","id":762111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=762104#post762104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have to check the backer pdf again, but I do know that in 2E all Solars had &quot;universal&quot; anima powers like lighting up the area or knowing the time. Perhaps a temporary illusion like this could be something similar for 3E Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Lunars had that basic stuff too - only instead of knowing the exact time of day, they knew the exact time of the month/phase-of-the-moon. Temporary Illusion Disguises are way too major a power for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T03:50:09-08:00","id":763929,"title":"","content":"The bit about not impersonating a specific character strikes me as worded in a somewhat unclear manner - would a disguise fail because someone, somewhere looks exactly like that? I would rather say that the Lunar can attempt to impersonate someone, but the likeness is imperfect and close friends can tell the difference (though they too would find the resemblance uncanny). It would be good to have an upgraded version where a Lunar CAN in fact do a perfect copy of someone s/he knows and is close to. What I am going for is the possibility for the Lunar to function as a body double of a close friend, mate or someone else important to them. Maybe it could require a symbolic bonding ritual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T03:59:17-08:00","id":763932,"title":"","content":"You could've just fucked 'em in 2E and then added their form to your Heart's Blood. I actually think this is rather fitting if the aim is to be the body double of your Solar mate, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T04:04:56-08:00","id":763936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>4uk4ata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=763929#post763929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bit about not impersonating a specific character strikes me as worded in a somewhat unclear manner - would a disguise fail because someone, somewhere looks exactly like that? I would rather say that the Lunar can attempt to impersonate someone, but the likeness is imperfect and close friends can tell the difference (though they too would find the resemblance uncanny). It would be good to have an upgraded version where a Lunar CAN in fact do a perfect copy of someone s/he knows and is close to. What I am going for is the possibility for the Lunar to function as a body double of a close friend, mate or someone else important to them. Maybe it could require a symbolic bonding ritual?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2nd ed, the Ebon Dragon impersonation charm had this clause. It just meant people looked almost exactly like someone, but with a mole. Your fix seems reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T04:54:08-08:00","id":763954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/413424-hatewheel-has-a-lunar-question?p=763932#post763932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could've just fucked 'em in 2E and then added their form to your Heart's Blood. I actually think this is rather fitting if the aim is to be the body double of your Solar mate, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is also a decent option, having charms or knacks that offer other ways to add someone you are really interested into to your Heart\u00b4s Blood forms. As long as you have a way to impersonate perfectly someone without having eating their heart or having fucked /bit them in the last couple of hours, it would be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3332-4uk4ata","name":"4uk4ata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:39:22-08:00","id":764005,"title":"","content":"Yeah I don't mean to disagree with people saying this is a narrative/mechanical niche so far left empty - Lunars do at the moment have to fuck or kill someone to impersonate them, which can be rather impractical.<br /> On the other hand, this might be a feature, rather than a bug. Shapechanging is very powerful and I get wanting to have limitations on what it can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:51:09-08:00","id":764015,"title":"","content":"Eating/fucking does stop my Lunar from picking up forms (I mean, he could do that, but, you know, it's wrong), but the Lunar knack for consuming other Lunars does also let you learn forms from other Lunars (at 1xp per form) so I use that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T08:04:40-08:00","id":764060,"title":"","content":"I think when you've got a group in which being able to transform into other shapes is a core, universal thing, and give them the placement in the setting that the Lunars do, a few obstacles to being able to become just anybody, especially a person who already exists and has a certain measure of authority, is kind of necessary.<br /> <br /> Discussion of Lunars has too much of an assumption that shapeshifting should essentially mean that there are no effective defences against them as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T08:52:48-08:00","id":764106,"title":"","content":"The big problem with all the &quot;limit the Lunars' shapeshifting&quot; discussions is that, while it's totally a valid concern for a PC option, it means that the &quot;not-PC options&quot; and the options which have it only as a side trick sometimes have better shapeshifting, cheaper. In 2E, the spirit charm for it could easily outstrip anything Lunars could do, with far fewer restrictions. Even some single-purpose disguise charms belonging to other Exalted types do it better (oft due to the Tell in 2E).<br /> <br /> So I hope that thought is given both to the Lunars' powers, so they're as potent as they should be, AND to the side-powers of other splats and supernatural types, so they don't accidentally do it BETTER for less investment and complexity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}